---
term: Demotion
section: evolution-and-protection
order: 120
definition: A parent's act of moving a member charter back to a lower tier or to associate status.
seeAlso:
  - intervention
  - associative-consolidation
  - status
---
Demotion is [[associative consolidation]] run in reverse by the parent, without the charter's agreement. The demoted charter loses the rights of its former tier but keeps a [[contract]] with the parent, so it stays an [[associate]].

Without arbitrated terms, demotion takes the form of sanctions.
